  "rationale": "The changeset evolves the CFA3-owned shared CUDA compatibility core to structured IR V2, bounded runtime/build compatibility inspection, AMD HIP lowering and Intel SYCL-primary/OpenCL-secondary lowering. Spectral Compute SCALE is neither built nor loaded. The release-included native provider now has explicit Apache-2.0 License & Rights descriptor coverage while external target toolchain rights remain separate. Fresh exact-head positive, negative and rollback execution on supported physical AMD and Intel target hosts remains required before runtime promotion; no simulated PASS is claimed.",
